  <prompt>Make every stamp's BFF app registration carry authenticationBehaviors.removeUnverifiedEmailClaim = true, set by H3 and verified by H13.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 H3 and H13).</role>

  <goal>
    R3 task 047 binds a workforce sign-in to an existing contact by the token `email` claim
    (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalRegistrationEndpoints.cs:253`,
    `Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ContactIdentityBinder.cs`). That is safe only when the BFF app registration has
    `authenticationBehaviors.removeUnverifiedEmailClaim = true`; otherwise a user in an allowed customer directory with an
    unverified-domain email equal to a contact's email can register as that contact. Today no stamp sets or checks it
    (ACME's `spaarke-bff-api-acme` reads `authenticationBehaviors: null`). After this task H3 sets it on new and existing
    registrations (get-before-set, read back) and H13 trap T7 fails a stamp whose BFF app does not carry it.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Source: GitHub #2001 (SPA-r3 ISS-013); coordination note
      `notes/coordination/2026-10-13-from-spa-r3-adr028-a9-workforce-signin.md` rows 6 and 9.
      API surface, verified 2026-10-22: Microsoft Learn documents `authenticationBehaviors` as beta, but Graph **v1.0**
      returns and accepts it (live read-only GET on the dev BFF app `1e40baad` returns `{"removeUnverifiedEmailClaim": true}`
      via v1.0), and the control plane's Microsoft.Graph 6.5.0 (v1.0) SDK has
      `Application.AuthenticationBehaviors.RemoveUnverifiedEmailClaim`. Use the v1.0 SDK; no beta call.
      `authenticationBehaviors` is a complex type, so a PATCH replaces it whole: carry the current
      `BlockAzureADGraphAccess` and `RequireClientServicePrincipal` values over unchanged.
      The multitenant SPA client `5859e812` (Spaarke Workforce SPA) already has the flag (read 2026-10-22) — a one-time
      operator setting, not per stamp; H3 never touches it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner.cs (reference: PlanAcctOptionalClaim + EnsureAcctOptionalClaimAsync, lines ~753-858; step (2c) in ProvisionAsync)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/EntraAppReg/EntraAppRegRejectionCodes.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/CustomerIdentityT7Probe.cs (extend)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/GraphAppRoleParityT3Probe.cs (reference: tenant-scoped Graph read, I5)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/** (existing PlanAcctOptionalClaim and CustomerIdentityT7Probe tests)</file>
      <file>docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md (H3 and H13 T7 rows)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="§11">Extend existing surface: a new ensure step in GraphAppRegistrationProvisioner and a new clause in T7. No new interface, gate, DI registration or rejection-code family beyond one H3 code.</constraint>
    <constraint source="I5">The H13 Graph read is tenant-scoped to request.TenantId (the T3 pattern), never an ambient credential.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">No live change in this task. ACME's BFF app is fixed separately with the owner's OK.</constraint>
    <constraint source="H3">Only this customer's own app object is PATCHed; a registration already carrying true sends no PATCH.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">H3: internal static planner `PlanRemoveUnverifiedEmailClaim(AuthenticationBehaviors? current)` → null when already true, else a new object with RemoveUnverifiedEmailClaim = true and the other two values copied; `EnsureRemoveUnverifiedEmailClaimAsync` (fresh GET with replication retry, PATCH, read back with retry) as step (2d) after the acct claim; rejection code `appreg-unverified-email-claim-failed`; file-header paragraph.</step>
    <step order="2">H13 T7: read the BFF app registration (`applications(appId='{BffAppRegId}')`, select authenticationBehaviors) in request.TenantId; Failed when not true (null, false, missing); InfraFault on a Graph read error or a blank BffAppRegId; header OUTCOMES updated.</step>
    <step order="3">Unit tests: planner (null, false, true, other-values preserved); T7 pure decision for true / false / null. Update guide rows. dotnet test the control-plane tests.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">PlanRemoveUnverifiedEmailClaim returns null for current = { RemoveUnverifiedEmailClaim = true } and a PATCH body with true for null, false and an object with only other values set; BlockAzureADGraphAccess and RequireClientServicePrincipal are preserved.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H3 calls the ensure step for new and existing registrations; a write not observed on read back returns Failure with `appreg-unverified-email-claim-failed`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">T7 returns Failed for a BFF app with authenticationBehaviors null or removeUnverifiedEmailClaim false, Passed only when it is true and the existing Customer__Id / workforce-list clauses pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: T7 never Passes when the Graph read fails (InfraFault, not Passed); no beta endpoint string appears in the change.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

